# smartd on the K15 - SMART for the USB-attached media drive.
#
# Copy to the install dir and register the service (both need Administrator):
#   copy k15\smartd.conf.example "%PROGRAMFILES%\smartmontools\bin\smartd.conf"
#   "%PROGRAMFILES%\smartmontools\bin\smartd.exe" install
#   Start-Service smartd
#
# The device number is Windows' physical disk number, NOT a stable id. Confirm
# it before trusting this file, and again after any enclosure change:
#   smartctl --scan
#
# -d sat   the ASMedia 174c:55aa bridge needs SCSI/ATA translation. Auto-detect
#          finds it today; naming it means a firmware change fails loudly
#          rather than silently monitoring nothing.
# -a       all attributes, health, and the error log.
# -o on    offline data collection; -S on attribute autosave.
# -s       short test daily 02:00, long test the 1st of the month at 03:00. The
#          long test reads all 14 TB and takes ~23 h at low priority, so it is
#          monthly, not weekly.
# -W       temperature: log a 2 degree move, warn at 50, critical at 55. The
#          MG07's operating ceiling is 55.
# -m <nomailer> -M exec   no SMTP anywhere; every warning runs the script,
#          which emits one event that Alloy already ships.
#
# Append -M test for ONE restart to prove the alert chain end to end; a
# service that is merely running proves nothing. Remove it afterwards.
#
# Quote the path ONLY if it contains a space. smartd splits the line on
# whitespace before parsing -M, so a quoted path with no space in it never
# reaches a second token and dies on 'missing closing quote'.
#
# EDIT THIS PATH. It must be the live checkout on the K15 - smartd runs with
# system32 as its working directory, so a relative path silently never fires.
/dev/pd1 -d sat -a -o on -S on -s (S/../.././02|L/../01/./03) -W 2,50,55 -m <nomailer> -M exec C:\Users\minipc\Desktop\slopstation\k15\smart-alert.bat
